  "scoreProvenance": [
    "Source MIDI tracks were inspected against the named score staves; staff labels do not claim contrapuntal voice separation. EXT: Bosworth 1896 and Universal 1910 piano editions. The source identifies the complete solo-piano Op. 3 No. 2, not Rachmaninoff's physical performing edition.",
    "Read content/listen/rachmaninoff-prelude-c-sharp-minor-victor-1921.mjs and cache/analysis/rachmaninoff-prelude-c-sharp-minor-victor-1921.txt. Same complete work; recording sections are coarse locators, not forced bar anchors. Historic transfer tuning and noise were inspected separately.",
    "MEAS: cached absolute-pitch features at 2.5–3.2 s identify the B-flat harmonic series (MIDI46/58/65/70/74/77); 3.9–4.4 s identifies A (57/64/69/73/76/79), and 5.5–6.2 s identifies D (50/62/69/74/78). The feature extractor's residual tuning estimate is -0.33 semitones. Apply a documented +1 nominal-semitone sounding-pitch correction to all four source staves for this supplied transfer, without changing the printed notation or claiming that Rachmaninoff transposed the work. The uncorrected candidate's numerical pass concealed an actual pitch mismatch and a late first anchor."
  ],
